<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What OraDiscuss collects and, more to the point, what it deliberately does not store: no customer database, no card details, and roadmap votes with no identifier at all."
  updated="August 2026"
>
  <h2>1. The short version</h2>
  <p>
    OraDiscuss keeps no customer database. Your email address lives with our email provider, your
    payment details live with Paddle, and neither is copied into a store of our own. That is a
    deliberate design decision rather than a promise about future good behaviour: the safest way to
    never leak personal data is to never hold it.
  </p>
  <p>We do not sell your data, and there is no advertising tracking on this site.</p>

  <h2>2. What is collected, and where it goes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Your email address</strong>, when you ask for the free kit or subscribe. It is sent
      directly to beehiiv, our email provider, together with a tag recording which form you used. It
      is not written to any database we operate.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Roadmap votes.</strong> When you vote for a course, your address goes to beehiiv and a
      counter for that course is incremented by one on our side. The counter holds a course name and
      a number. It holds no address, no name, no IP, and deliberately no hash of any of them, since
      a hashed email is still a derived personal identifier. The result is an interest signal that
      cannot be traced back to a person, including by us.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Purchase data</strong>, handled entirely by Paddle as Merchant of Record. We never see
      or store your card details. Paddle does, as a PCI DSS compliant processor.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Membership access.</strong> To recognise a paying member without holding a customer
      record, we store a one-way hash derived from your Paddle transaction, never your email or
      name.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Technical logs</strong> kept by our hosting for security and operations, including IP
      address and request metadata, retained for a short period.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Diagnostic packs you download run on your own machine and write their output there. Their
    results are never transmitted to us. We do not receive your estate data, at any tier, ever.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Why we use it</h2>
  <p>
    To deliver what you asked for, to send the briefs and notifications you subscribed to, to grant
    and re-issue member downloads, to prevent abuse and fraud, and to meet legal obligations.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Who processes your data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong>: hosting, storage, security, and the bot check on our forms (global).</li>
    <li><strong>Paddle</strong>: payments, tax, invoicing and Merchant of Record (UK and global).</li>
    <li><strong>beehiiv</strong>: the email list and member sends (USA and global).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    That is the whole list. If it grows, this page changes before the provider is used, not
    afterwards.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Bot protection on forms</h2>
  <p>
    Our forms use Cloudflare Turnstile to tell a person from a script. It is a privacy-preserving
    alternative to a CAPTCHA: it does not track you across sites and it does not ask you to label
    photographs.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    Only what is strictly necessary to run the site and the bot check. No advertising cookies, no
    cross-site tracking, and no consent banner, because there is nothing to consent to.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Retention</h2>
  <p>
    Your subscription to the list lasts until you unsubscribe, which you can do from any email we
    send. Transaction records are retained by Paddle under its own retention and accounting
    obligations. Our own technical logs are short-lived. Roadmap counters are permanent but contain
    no personal data to retain.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:support@oradiscuss.com">support@oradiscuss.com</a> to access, correct,
    export, or delete your data, or to unsubscribe. If you are in the EU or UK you have the rights
    granted by GDPR and UK GDPR; if you are in California you have those granted by CCPA. We honour
    them regardless of where you live.
  </p>
  <p>
    One honest limitation: a roadmap vote cannot be individually deleted, because nothing in that
    counter identifies you. There is no row of yours to find. Your email address in the list can of
    course be removed at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>9. International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Your data may be processed in the United States, the United Kingdom, and elsewhere by the
    providers listed above, under the safeguards those providers maintain.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Security</h2>
  <p>
    Traffic is encrypted in transit. Member downloads are issued as short-lived signed links rather
    than public files. Our largest single control is the one described at the top: the data we do
    not hold cannot be taken from us.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Children</h2>
  <p>
    This is a professional tool for working database administrators. It is not directed at anyone
    under 18, and we do not knowingly collect data from children.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    The date at the top changes when this policy does. Material changes are announced to members by
    email.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Privacy questions and data requests go to
    <a href="mailto:support@oradiscuss.com">support@oradiscuss.com</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
